WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
ONS figures: in the
year ending March 2023,

2
00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:09.090
UK net migration peaked at 944,000.

3
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:15.450
By the year ending December
2025, it had fallen to 171,000.

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.340
And the longer view?

5
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:22.390
UN estimates put migrants living
in the UK at 3.66 million in 1990,

6
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.850
and 11.85 million in 2024.

7
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.530
So when numbers swing that far, that fast,

8
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.830
who decides how many people come?

9
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.910
In this mission, you'll split the
UK's migration into who comes,

10
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.170
who goes, and why.

11
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.910
Then you'll trace the money and people
that tie the UK to other countries.

12
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:48.850
Your mission: find out who really
decides how many people come to the UK.
